values ('d8e9f0a1-2b3c-4e92-9b12-2f3a4b5c6d22', 'building-codes-and-regulations', 'Building Codes and Regulations', 'Students learn how American building regulation actually works: model codes become enforceable only through adoption, amendments, plan review, inspections, and the authority having jurisdiction. The course covers I-Code navigation, occupancy and mixed use, construction type and allowable area, fire and life safety, means of egress, accessibility and universal design, public-health and MEP coordination, energy codes, zoning and site constraints, existing buildings, code-analysis documentation, permitting, and professional responsibility. A capstone applies code analysis to a design and produces a review package with reasoning, drawings, and revisions.');

